+# Make a UI material
+> Make a UI material for an effect, built so it works the first time.
+Arguments: effect - what it should look like (e.g. "a soft purple glow that breathes", "scanlines scrolling down")
+Make a UI material for: {{effect}}. Work in this order and stop at the first that fits: (1) a library master instance - list_options material_masters, then create_material_instance with its parameters; (2) a master plus a few nodes - build_ui_material with from_master and graph ("master.FinalColor" is its color); (3) a new graph - list_options material_nodes once, then build_ui_material from macro nodes (glow, soft_circle, ring, rounded_rect, linear_gradient, radial_gradient, color_ramp, panning_noise, time_wave, uv_tile, band, stripes, remap) and a few maths nodes, every color, speed and size written as {"param": "Name", "value": v}. If it reports problems, fix all of them in one retry. Say which path you took and which parameters can be tuned.
